# The generated SDK IS committed, deliberately.
#
# It was gitignored at first, which left this repo with config files and no SDK: a clone was
# not browsable, not installable from a git URL, and required Docker to see anything. That is
# wrong for a client library, whatever its merits for a private prototype.
#
# Committing it is what Anthropic's and Stainless's SDK repos do, and it buys the thing that
# matters most in review: a spec change produces a readable diff showing what happened to the
# PUBLIC API. "This renamed a method" is exactly the change that is expensive to discover
# after publishing.
#
# Regenerate with `bun run generate` (pulls the live spec, then generates) and commit the
# result as its own commit, so machine-written diffs stay separate from hand-written ones.

# Keep the released OpenAPI snapshot so publication never reads a newer live spec.

# Fern working files
**/.preview
**/.definition

# Reproducible from source; node_modules would be tens of thousands of files.
node_modules/
sdks/typescript/node_modules/
sdks/typescript/dist/
sdks/typescript/package-lock.json
sdks/typescript/bun.lock

*.tgz
__pycache__/
